WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.200
All right.

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.134
We're learning that

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.502
Lisa Marie Presley

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.738
will be buried at Graceland in Memphis

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.906
next to her father, Elvis Presley,

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.475
and her son, Ben.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.442
A family spokesperson

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.910
made the announcement Friday.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.846
The only child of Elvis Presley

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.180
and Priscilla Presley

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.448
died Friday after suffering

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.916
cardiac arrest.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.419
Presley had a music career of her own

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:21.421
but was probably best known

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.089
for her marriage to pop

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.924
superstar Michael Jackson,

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.259
as she was also open

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.660
at times about her struggles

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.561
with addiction.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.431
Lisa Marie Presley was 54 years old,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.932
passing away this week.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.868
Let's bring in Alana Nash.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.835
She's a journalist

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.270
who has written several books

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:37.971
about the life

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.406
and times of Elvis Presley.

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.274
Including The Colonel,

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.443
The Extraordinary Story of Colonel Tom

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.612
Parker and Elvis Presley.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.313
So good to see you, Alana.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.117
Thank you so much for having me here.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:51.684
So I'm wondering,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.620
what was your reaction

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.523
when you heard the news of Lisa Marie's

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.690
passing

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.828
Oh, deep, deep sadness.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.363
It really shook me,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.230
I think,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.266
not only because I had interviewed her

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.700
and been around her a little bit

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.271
and enjoyed her music, but also just that

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.473
the Presley story is one of,

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.310
you know, great opportunity and wealth

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:18.511
and fame

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.612
but that just equals

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.981
sadness and trauma and tragedy

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.583
that balance that out.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.252
And I think we wanted her to be happy

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.054
and have a joyful life

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.189
because her father had

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.490
given us so much joy.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.892
So there's there's deep sadness

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.994
about her passing all over the world.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:35.361
Yeah.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.629
And since you had an opportunity

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.330
to speak with her

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.832
on so many occasions, and,

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:39.032
you know,

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.500
and you talk about how collectively

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.602
everybody want to be happy and be joyful,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.536
but then what

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.637
did you sense

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.473
from her in your conversations with her

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.541
about what was keeping her

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:48.842
what was

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:52.445
in the way of that joy and happiness that

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.747
everybody would wish for her?

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.351
I think just the

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.686
crushing weight

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:03.089
of fame, number one, and loss and grief,

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.757
you know, the

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.794
there's a lot of a long line of loss

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.362
and grief on on her father's

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.597
mother's side.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.699
And it seems to be continuing

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.868
through the generations.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.202
I think she always wanted

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.670
that sense of peace

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.306
and family unity and search for that.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.475
Loved being a mother,

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:22.842
loved

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.644
being part of the rock and roll world,

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.278
but just

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.614
could not find lasting happiness.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.550
She she loved it.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.418
But at the same time,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.889
was she all also kind of disdainful

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.024
you know, of

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:41.461
the celebrity, especially learning

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.495
as she has over

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.163
the years

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.398
about the people surrounding her dad?

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:48.067
And she was a part of this.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.670
This latest, you know, blockbuster film

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.440
in which, you know, she got to enjoy,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.975
you know, the actor

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.710
getting a Golden Globe this week.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.445
But there was there was something

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.081
that also made her very uncomfortable,

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.050
angry, if that's the right word.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.585
Or you better describe for me

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.887
what what she thought of, you know,

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.722
the world of entertainment

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.226
Well, she was certainly

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.061
an angry little girl.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.063
And you see that

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.498
in a lot of her photographs.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.599
And you certainly see it

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:20.800
when she became an artist.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.367
And again,

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.802
writing songs,

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.704
those those songs are just filled

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.306
with acrimony and bitterness,

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:28.474
but also with with a really sardonic

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:29.542
black humor,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.710
a kind of sense of humor

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.812
that balance that out

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.447
made it very appealing.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.249
But she was never really comfortable

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:36.983
in public.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.184
She loved the fans.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:38.751
But she

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.419
she looked

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.587
at fame

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.121
as a thief that stole

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.323
everything that mattered.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.791
And so she was that she was always

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.026
jumping and. Wow.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:47.961
And at the same time,

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.295
did she feel like

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.331
I mean, she was compelled to also

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.533
just try her hand

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.736
at having a relationship with fame

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.973
by being a singer herself?

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:04.110
And if she felt like she had to do that?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.912
Or was it like her?

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.181
I mean, was it her feeling that

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.549
she couldn't,

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.451
you know, part from that,

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:11.684
you know,

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.419
because of the legacy of her dad?

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:13.686
I mean,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.121
what was it that compelled her

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.223
even though she had this disdain,

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.691
also say, well,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.993
I'm going to also reach

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:23.062
into my musical roots and try my hand

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:26.366
at that end of fame.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.534
Well, it was a part of her.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.570
While she was enormously proud

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.537
of being

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.639
daughter

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:33.273
that wanted

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.942
to step outside of that shadow,

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:36.576
you see that,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.011
I think in her marriage

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:40.146
to Michael Jackson, King of Pop.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.581
You see that

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.182
perhaps in her brief marriage

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.484
to Nicolas Cage,

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:45.752
but also to

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.152
two men

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.520
who were not involved

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.555
in high stakes business.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.125
But she was a deep and true artist

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.359
like like her father.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:53.926
But of course,

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:57.196
there was no real escaping that shadow.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.800
And then and then it sounds like there's

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.235
no escaping the loss

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:02.769
and the grief

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.570
that you were just describing to

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.039
with the suicide death

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:08.675
of her own son, Ben.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:09.942
What kind of impact did

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.044
that make on her life?

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.481
She said it destroyed her.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.482
And, you know,

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.451
I think that's probably right.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.552
You see this

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:20.586
dichotomy of her,

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.455
of a lot of strength of character

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.790
but fragility.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.624
She always seemed

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.459
kind of like a lost little girl

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.361
who needed a lot of protecting.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.496
And that increased with the death

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.464
of her son

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.466
in 20, 20

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.500
And, you know, he looked a lot

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.702
like Elvis as well.

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.770
He knew Lisa. My gosh.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.007
What she does was it eyes and bright

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:43.676
blue eyes and beauty Oh, my goodness.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.545
I mean, it is so shocking and sad.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:45.912
I think

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:46.879
even this many days

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.381
after the fact, it's still,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.484
you know, really hard, you know, to

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.420
to to understand you grieve for her,

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:55.254
you know,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.123
and the more we're learning about what

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:57.724
she has been

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.058
through her entire life

00:05:59.058 --> 00:05:59.492
after her

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.594
dad's passing at the age of nine.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:02.161
I mean, it's

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.831
just been so traumatic on so many levels.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.232
And you helped really fill

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.734
in a lot of blanks for us.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.469
Lana Nash, thank you so much.

